            <ArticleTitle>[Populational characteristics of metabolic syndrome in open male population].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>58-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">to assess prevalence of various clusters of metabolic syndrome (MS) in open male population aged 25- 64 years.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">This cross sectional epidemiological study was conducted on a representative population sample formed from lists of male voters in one of administrative districts in Tumen. NCEP ATP III (2004) MS criteria were used in analysis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Prevalences of MS were different in various 20 year age intervals. Most frequent 3-component MS variant (5.6%) was combination of arterial hypertension, abdominal obesity, and hyperglycemia; combination of these factors with hypertriglyceridemia was most frequent 4-componet variant (1.5%).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
